  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Arrows",
      "items": [
        "An arrow between two packages is a project reference that PackageGraph allows, from the package that references to the one it references; these are all of this view's references. The two arrows into PostgreSQL are data access, not references: Persistence.Postgres writes, Persistence.Dapper reads.",
        "PackageGraphTests checks each package's direct references and restored closure against PackageGraph.",
        "PouryaKit.Messaging.Wolverine.EFCore belongs to the messaging and delivery view; it appears here because PouryaKit.Testing references it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What the core packages add",
      "items": [
        "PouryaKit.Cqrs holds commands, queries, their handlers, the dispatcher and its fixed pipeline, the Operation and its Operation Context, IUnitOfWork, and the composition checks a Host runs when its container is built.",
        "Validation, Security, Observability and Caching each fill one seam of that pipeline: the validation step, the authorization hook, a decorator around the dispatcher, and the query cache slot.",
        "Persistence.EFCore implements IUnitOfWork of Cqrs and IRepository of Persistence; Persistence.Postgres puts a Module's DbContext in its own schema on PostgreSQL.",
        "Persistence.Dapper reads plain SQL on the Host's pooled connection, outside the Unit of Work, and reads a Cqrs PageRequest into a Page.",
        "Web begins each HTTP request's Operation through Cqrs; Web.OpenApi, optional, versions each Module's route group.",
        "Security.JwtBearer references Security alone; the tenant claim type it writes is PouryaKitClaimTypes of PouryaKit.Cqrs, reached through Security.",
        "Cqrs, Security, Web, Persistence.EFCore and Persistence.Dapper reference PouryaKit.Core for its helpers, such as ImplementingTypes.",
        "Storage, the file storage contract, references Domain, and Cqrs for its one-provider composition check; Storage.S3 and Storage.AzureBlob, its providers, reference Storage and their cloud SDK, and a Host registers exactly one of them.",
        "Localization, optional, records a Module's Feature assemblies through Cqrs and sets each request's culture, English or Persian, from its Accept-Language header; the Proving Sample's Hosts reference none of it.",
        "Grpc maps a Module's gRPC services on Web's begin-the-Operation convention and writes a client's Operation Context through Web's one header codec; a failed Result is a status by its most severe Error kind.",
        "Aspire, AppHost-only, references no Kit package: an Aspire AppHost adds PostgreSQL, Redis and RabbitMQ through it, each on a pinned image with a named volume, and no other Kit package's closure holds an Aspire package.",
        "Reporting, optional, references Domain alone: it renders a Module's layout to a PDF, a CSV file or a spreadsheet and returns the file's bytes, storing nothing; QuestPDF, ClosedXML, a storage SDK and PouryaKit.Storage stay out of its closure.",
        "AI gives a Host one chat client over the OpenAI client, and makes a Module's command or query a Gateway tool: each call a model makes runs as an Operation through that Module's Gateway, which is why it references Modularity; no OllamaSharp, Azure client or resilience package reaches its closure."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
